# __PROJECT_NAME__

A [Maximus](https://github.com/getarbol/maximus) project: an API on Cloudflare Workers whose routes are also
MCP tools when they say so, configured in one file, `vite.config.ts`.

## Start

```sh
bun install
bun run dev
```

`GET /api/v1/greeting` answers `{ "message": "Hello World" }` to a signed-in caller. Locally, sign in with the
development token in `.dev.vars`, which `vp dev` accepts from localhost alone:

```sh
curl -H "authorization: Bearer $(cut -d= -f2 .dev.vars)" http://localhost:5173/api/v1/greeting
```

`/api/openapi.json` describes the API and `/health` reports liveness.

## Build on it

| Add                      | How                                                                         |
| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| A route                  | `bunx maximus gen route get /v1/tasks/{taskId}` writes its file in routes/  |
| A tool only agents call  | `bunx maximus gen tool summarize-tasks` writes mcp/tools/summarize-tasks.ts |
| A binding (KV, D1, …)    | `env: { TASKS: bindings.kv() }` in maximus(), from `cf/config`              |
| Your own failures        | `errors.ts` default-exports `defineErrors({ … })`                           |
| What every handler needs | `context.ts` default-exports `defineContext(…)`                             |

`.maximus/` is generated from these files on every `vp dev` and `vp build`; never edit it.

## Verify and deploy

`bun run verify` runs the types, lint and format, the tests and the build. Before the first deployment, set
`origin` to the Worker's HTTPS URL (its workers.dev URL or a custom domain you own) and `tokens.issuer` to
your authorization server. Then:

```sh
bunx cf auth login
bun run deploy
```

The GitHub workflow verifies every pull request and deploys `main` with the repository secrets
`CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`.
